erweight and Obesity in Canada: A Population Health Perspective</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Ottawa, Ontario:Canadian Institute for Health Information</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Trakas</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawrence</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Shear</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Utilization of health care resources by obese Canadians</article-title><source>CMAJ</source><year>1999</year><volume>160</volume><fpage>1457</fpage><lpage>1462</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10352635</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tjepkema</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adult obesity in Canada: Measured height and weight. Statistics Canada</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.statcan.ca/english/research/82-620-MIE/2005001/articles/adults/aobesity.htm"/><comment>accessed July 5, 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organization</collab></person-group><article-title>Obesity : Preventing and Managing the Global Epidemic</article-title><source>Report of a WHO Consultation on Obesity</source><year>2000</year><volume>894</volume><publisher-name>Geneva: World Health Organization</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>253</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ogden</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Carroll</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Flegal</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemiologic trends in overweight and ob